			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Complete webview-view lifecycle, patch terminal backend, stabilize PostHog ID\n\nSubmodule synchronization bringing three major improvements:\n\n1. Webview Notification Channels (Mountain + Sky + Output):\n   - Mountain adds `cocoon:notify` handler as fire-and-forget companion to existing request/response bridge, handling one-way methods (webview.message, webview.dispose, webview.viewState) without 30s timeout\n   - Extends webview notification relay to handle `webview.updateView` and `webview.reveal` in addition to setTitle/setIconPath/setHtml\n   - Sky adds `sky://webview/updateView` handler and workbench→extension event forwarding (message, viewState, dispose) completing the full lifecycle: register → resolve → set-html → update-metadata → communicate → dispose\n   - Output exposes IWebviewViewService on globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__.WebviewViews enabling SkyBridge to register resolvers for extension sidebar/panel webviews\n\n2. Terminal Backend Patch (Output):\n   - Add PatchLocalTerminalBackend transform bypassing Electron's acquirePort that never resolves under Tauri/WKWebView\n   - Routes pty operations through existing _localPtyService channel proxy (localPty:* handlers)\n   - Fixes terminal createProcess/attachToProcess calls hanging forever\n\n3. PostHog Identifier Stability (Sky + Wind):\n   - Sky adds GetOrCreateSkyIdentifier() generating persistent `land-dev-sky-{8-char-random}` stored in localStorage\n   - Wind fixes fallback to use username from USER/USERNAME env vars instead of Date.now()\n   - Ensures consistent device tracking across editor sessions\n\nImpact: Extension webview panels now render correctly, terminal PTYs spawn under Tauri, and telemetry correctly tracks unique users/devices.",
			"SHA": "dbe3e3b738cc8e34999de7128fc809b62b1f1e1f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:03:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Align webview.setHtml channel between Mountain and Sky\n\nSynchronized submodule update fixing webview-view extension API communication:\n\n1. Mountain adds suffix mapping to translate VS Code's camelCase `webview.setHtml` to Sky's canonical kebab-case `set-html` channel. This ensures events route correctly to `sky://webview/set-html` where Sky's listener expects them.\n\n2. Sky adds two new handlers completing the webview-view lifecycle:\n   - `sky://webview/set-html` - applies HTML to parked workbench WebviewView from `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS__`\n   - `sky://webview/postMessage` - forwards extension messages to the parked view's webview\n\nThis is the final piece of the channel alignment series (following Terminal, Debug, StatusBar, Progress, Output), enabling extensions like GitLens to properly render their sidebar panels.",
			"SHA": "271252d910f0d1a555fcf6b7ea42d4acaf909fc4"
		}
